00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:44.620
week. And that speeds up RCNN quite a bit. It turns out that one of the problems with fast

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:50.460
RCNN algorithm is that the clustering step to propose the regions is still quite slow.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:56.060
And so a different group, Xiaoxing Ren, Kaimingher, Roscoe Schwick, and Jian Sun,

00:04:56.060 --> 00:05:02.380
proposed the faster RCNN algorithm which uses a convolutional neural network instead of one of

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:07.740
the more traditional segmentation algorithms to propose the blobs of proposed regions. And that

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:15.020
wound up running quite a bit faster than the fast RCNN algorithm. Although I think the faster RCNN

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:21.180
algorithm, most implementations are usually still quite a bit slower than the YOLO algorithm.

